WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 6 Student Video
Unit 2, Lesson 2: Monotheism

1
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:07.210
Think about the times where you have felt most connected to God.

2
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:13.070
Where was it? For many people, myself included, it's taken place on the top of a

3
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.790
mountain. There's just something about being in nature, higher than normal, away

4
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.890
from distractions, that we feel the presence of God.

5
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.090
There's something powerful and spiritual about being on the top of a mountain.

6
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.020
Interestingly, the great monotheistic religions all have traditions of a

7
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.300
formative experience for their founder on a mountaintop.

8
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.900
Take Judaism. Moses, arguably the most important prophet of the Old Testament,

9
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.040
both saw God face to face and received the law on a mountaintop.

10
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.760
In Islam, Muhammad, the founding prophet, claimed to receive the revelation

11
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.260
from the angel Gabriel, which he wrote down as verses or surahs.

12
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.620
In the Quran. And Jesus gave some of his most important teaching

13
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.320
on the Mount of Olives.

14
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.340
Like naturalism and pantheism, monotheism offers answers to our four big worldview

15
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:26.680
questions. And the first question is, what is real?

16
00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.820
Now in naturalism, you'll remember that only physical things exist.

17
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.840
On pantheism, all is divine. But on monotheism, there's both

18
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.120
physical and non-physical things.

19
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.180
There are material and immaterial entities.

20
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:50.240
So rocks, dirt, and trees and other physical things are very real.

21
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:56.240
But there's also a spiritual realm that includes God, angels, demons,

22
00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.360
and the soul.

23
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.680
The second worldview question is, what is man?

24
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.760
Rather than seeing man as the result of this blind, purposeless evolutionary process

25
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.520
as naturalism claims, or a part of the oneness of the universe as pantheism claims,

26
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:20.120
monotheism states that we are the purposeful creation of a loving and personal God.

27
00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.320
And we uniquely reflect his character and image.

28
00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:29.100
The third worldview question is, what happens at death?

29
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.360
According to naturalism, humans simply face extinction.

30
00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.880
According to pantheism, we go through some kind of reincarnation until we enter the

31
00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.540
oneness of the universe. But on monotheism, when we die, we face judgment based upon

32
00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.040
God's standards and how we lived our lives.

33
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.460
And then for eternity, we either go to heaven or we go to hell.

34
00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.660
The fourth worldview question is, what is the basis for right and wrong?

35
00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:02.660
And unlike in pantheism and naturalism, on monotheism, morality is not

36
00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:07.600
a human construct. Rather, morality comes from either the characteristics of God,

37
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.500
the character, or the commands of God.

38
00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.640
So there is a source outside of us that we are accountable to.

39
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.680
We don't get to decide what is right and wrong, but we do get to decide if we're

40
00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.720
going to follow it.

41
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.620
Essentially, monotheism says we are the purposeful creation of one God.

42
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.180
And our lives now and for eternity depend upon how we respond to this God.

43
00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.840
Now when we talk about monotheism, we're kind of talking about God in the abstract.

44
00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.980
The question is, has this one God made himself known?

45
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:52.020
Has this God stepped into creation and revealed his plan and purpose for

46
00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:52.260
mankind?

